  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal word used for official or professional observation visits. The subject is typically someone in a position of authority — a politician, executive, or expert. Not used for casual sightseeing or personal visits.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {視察|しさつ}する (to inspect, to observe)\n- {視察|しさつ}{団|だん} (inspection group, observation delegation)\n- {現地|げんち}{視察|しさつ} (on-site inspection)\n- {視察|しさつ}{報告|ほうこく} (inspection report)\n- {視察|しさつ}に{訪|おとず}れる (to visit for inspection)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {見学|けんがく}: study visit — less formal, often educational (e.g., factory tours for students)\n- {調査|ちょうさ}: investigation, survey — broader, includes data collection beyond observation\n- {点検|てんけん}: inspection — checking equipment or items for defects, not observing conditions",
